[{:seon.task/name "prove-runs-what-a-change-reaches"
  :seon.task/plan "What exists (merged; AGENTS.md §3 Testing and §5, results reused by input digest; design: notes/archive/fork-test-merge-design-2026-10-22.md §2): one of each. The selection `seon.proofs/plan`: a key runs exactly when no green is stored at its reach digest; with a base (an agent's branch against main at its merge base) it selects the proofs and the moved digests, without one the proofs and every key with no green. The digests `seon.program/reach-digests` (tests by default; bin/check steps by their seon.check functions through `seon.proofs/check-steps`, the one list bin/check reads from `./seon steps`; `seon.proofs/step-digests` names a step whose function is gone as missing, red). The runner `seon.proofs/run-tests!` (bin/test's shards and an agent's test fork). The results directory `:seon.config.source/test-results-dir` (`seon.proofs/greens`, `seon.proofs/store!` through `seon.fx/write-file`). Entry points: `bin/prove` for worktree sessions and root (`bin/test` and `bin/check` without arguments are its halves; `bin/check --steps DIR`), and `seon.agent/test-plan` for an agent's run (the turn's observe, the reconciler's :tests, the merge gate, `(my.agent/prove)`); full runs are explicit (`bin/test --all`, `bin/check 100`); a merge runs bin/prove on the merged tree (docs/merging.md#a-merge-runs-what-the-change-reaches, with the measurements). Deleted: `bin/test --reach` and test-runner's plan, run-vars!, reach-main and green?; `seon.agent/test-vars`; `seon.program/reaching-tests`. Shards are processes bin/test starts, not forks of the runner (a forked child of the jolt test runtime hangs at its first d/connect). The digest's inputs: quoted names by namespace, `seon.program/env-readers`, a test's form reached only as its own root, system.edn's procs as data refs (`seon.fx/declared-refs`), a test running the binary only through `seon.test-store/binary-sh`, and the config in force (`test-runner/config-input`). Agents: the source tree's inputs (`seon.fx/inputs`, the one producer, also bin/test's) are read by `seon.fx/read-source` on an effect worker and written on the boot's `:seon.root/source` fact (`seon.root/import-source!`) only when the running binary is built from that tree (`target/seon.tree`, `seon.fx/tree-id`), else `:unshared` says why; an agent uses only its root's current boot's inputs and keeps its greens in the shared results directory (:seon.config.source/test-results-dir) through root's :file owner: the owner ruled (2026-10-23) that a test that is the same is not run again once green, \"especially when freshly branched\", so an agent's greens and a checkout's are one store (seon.agent-test/an-agents-greens-and-a-checkouts-are-one-store). A shard compares the planned tree before storing, so an edit during a run never stores a green under the unedited digests. v1 keyed a result by its reach digest (~/src/seon seon.test.cache). Open: shards are balanced by test count, not time; seon.source-test/a-restart-catches-up-and-a-new-generation-resumes waits on an `nc -w 600` that never times out an idle connection on macOS."
  :seon.task/kind :work
  :seon.task/needs #{"seon.program/refs-name-quoted-symbols-and-macro-uses"}
  :seon.task/proofs #{seon.proofs-test/an-unchanged-tree-runs-nothing-and-reuses-everything
                      seon.proofs-test/a-one-defn-change-runs-only-what-reaches-it
                      seon.proofs-test/a-macro-schema-or-config-change-widens-the-selection
                      seon.proofs-test/a-check-step-is-keyed-by-what-its-function-reaches
                      seon.proofs-test/shards-split-by-namespace-and-each-result-is-stored
                      seon.proofs-test/selection-is-proportional-to-what-changed
                      seon.program-test/only-a-test-reading-the-tree-takes-its-digest
                      seon.program-test/the-same-tree-gives-the-same-digests-in-any-checkout-and-any-run
                      seon.program-test/a-test-naming-another-test-does-not-reach-it
                      seon.proofs-test/a-failed-write-or-a-throwing-fixture-is-recorded-red
                      seon.agent-test/a-wide-reach-reuses-unchanged-results}}
 {:seon.task/name "the-judge-reads-run-tests-results"
  :seon.task/plan "What exists: an agent's run carries clojure.test's report format end to end: `seon.agent/run-tests-here` collects each assertion as a report map (`seon.agent/test-report`), and the judge and the turn read them back through `seon.proofs/results`, `seon.proofs/red-reports`, `seon.proofs/failures`, `seon.proofs/run-errors` and `seon.proofs/costs`, while `seon.proofs/run-tests!` already answers one result per test ({:test :digest :pass :fail :error :ms}, a throw's :message and :data). Correct: the judge (`seon.reconcile/done-explain`'s input), the turn (`seon.turn/observe`), the attempt's facts (:seon.attempt/failures, :seon.attempt/costs) and the context read run-tests!'s result map, each red test keeping its failing assertions (expected, actual, got); the report vector, `test-report` and the readers that rebuild a status per test from it go. About -30 lines in src. Proofs: the done error, the attempt's failures and costs, and the context's red block read the same from the result map as today from the reports."
  :seon.task/kind :work
  :seon.task/needs #{"seon.proofs/prove-runs-what-a-change-reaches"}}
 {:seon.task/name "turn-logic-from-recorded-data"
  :seon.task/plan "Owner, 2026-10-23: tests shouldn't be running agent turns. A run that names nothing leaves out the tests and steps that reach a process (test-runner/automatic over seon.program/reach-index's :process?; notes/process-tests-2026-10-23.md), so what they cover is proven only when named, in the full run or at root's gate. Where the covered logic is a function of data, test it without a process: the reconciler's step from a recorded fact state (seon.reconcile/reconciler-proc on a db holding the attempt facts, as procs-test does), the merge from two dbs (seon.merge/three-way, global-ids' delta-three-way), the context render from a recorded basis (seon.context on a :seon.turn/basis), the agent-proc step from recorded events, seon.server/respond on recorded requests, the help page's and templates' forms through seon.repl's handler in process, the restart catch-up as load-all! over a db holding two merges. Each new unit test names the process test whose logic it carries; the process test stays as the end-to-end check, run when named. Measured: the process tests were 90 of 443 tests and 782 of their 917 s (2026-10-23 full run)."
  :seon.task/kind :work
  :seon.task/proofs #{seon.proofs-test/a-run-that-names-nothing-leaves-out-what-reaches-a-process}}
 {:seon.task/name "a-nested-runs-reports-reach-only-its-run"
  :seon.task/plan "What exists: `seon.proofs/run-tests!` counts its own tests through its report binding and passes every report on to clojure.test's default report (`seon.proofs/report`, the root value captured at load), so the outer binding is never used. That report bumps whatever tally is in force (Jolt's stdlib clojure/test.clj, `inc-report-counter` and `fail!`): an enclosing t/run-tests' *report-counters* when one is bound, else Jolt's process-wide `counters` atom (`global-tally?`). So a test that runs tests of its own, such as seon.proofs-test/shards-split-by-namespace-and-each-result-is-stored with its deliberate (is (= 1 2)) in app.pv-red-test, adds that fail to the caller's tally. Under t/run-tests the outer test reads red (found by pure-tests, 2026-10-23); under bin/test it is green, because test-runner reads run-tests!'s own counts, but Jolt's process tally (n-fail, failures) still carries the inner fail. Cause: the nested run has no tally of its own. Correct: run-tests! binds clojure.test/*report-counters* to a ref of its own around its test-vars, so a nested run's reports land in that ref and nowhere else (Jolt's global-tally? is false for a caller-bound ref); its results stay its volatiles. Replaces nothing; +1 binding. Proofs: shards-split… is green under t/run-tests as under bin/test, and Jolt's process tally reads the same before and after it."
  :seon.task/kind :work
  :seon.task/proofs #{seon.proofs-test/shards-split-by-namespace-and-each-result-is-stored}}
 {:seon.task/name "one-reach-walk-a-plan"
  :seon.task/plan "Done (worktree session reuse, 2026-10-23, task seon.derive/one-content-keyed-derivation's cold paths). What existed: test-runner/plan-of built the reach graph twice a plan, once in tests-of (seon.program/reach-index over every test) and again for the bin/check steps (reach-index with the steps' roots), though the graph (seon.program/reach-graph) is the same value and only seon.program/graph-index differs by roots. Measured on the whole tree (src and test, 2,769 forms): one reach-graph is 232M ticks and 912 MB. Fix at the cause: tests-of builds the graph once and hands it on (:graph), and plan-of reads the steps' index from it (graph-index). A plan of tests and steps: 2.88G ticks and 8.8 GB before, 2.65G ticks and 7.9 GB after (8% of the plan). What is left of the plan is the import into a db (seon.source/import-tx 510M ticks, 3.2 GB; d/db-with 1.9G ticks, 3.7 GB, the store session's). Replaces the second walk; deletes nothing else."
  :seon.task/kind :work
  :seon.task/proofs #{seon.proofs-test/a-run-that-names-nothing-leaves-out-what-reaches-a-process}}
 {:seon.task/name "a-plan-keeps-a-program-db-per-tree"
  :seon.task/plan "Done (worktree session reuse, 2026-10-23; the owner's option B, notes/test-fork-main-2026-10-23.md). What existed: test-runner/program-db imported the whole of src and test into the in-memory test store on every plan (seon.source/import-tx, then d/db-with): on today's main a plan of tests and steps was 1.94G ticks warm (6.1 s CPU), and transacting the import into LMDB alone 1.43G ticks (4.2 s) even after jolt/datom-cost. The program db is a function of the git tree, so it is kept per tree: one LMDB store per checkout (:seon.config.proofs/program-store, target/program-store), a branch per tree id (seon.fx/tree-id, git's content address, never updated). The same tree reads its branch; a tree never seen is branched from the kept tree with the fewest changed program files (git diff --name-only, trees in the checkout's own repository) and brought current by seon.source/refresh-tx; only an empty store imports the whole program. Bounded in bytes (:seon.config.proofs/program-store-max-bytes): past it a run keeps only its own tree and collects, deterministic. Measured: d/branch! 2 ms, a one-file refresh-tx 6 ms and its transact 23 ms; the store 12 MB for the whole program, ~2 MB more a kept tree with one changed file; a kept tree's program db 1.17M ticks and 4.6 MB whatever the program's size (the cost proof); bin/test's selection 1.65 s on an unchanged tree and 1.7 s after a one-file edit, against ~15 s with an empty store. What is left of a plan is the reach graph (~240M ticks, ~1 s). Tests that built a whole program db (program-test, agent-test, main-test) take this process's own store (seon.test-store/program-store). Deletes the per-run import and the runner's note that a fork cannot connect to a store. Option A, a worktree's root answering through seon_prove, stays the end state: this is its tree-to-branch step."
  :seon.task/kind :work
  :seon.task/proofs #{seon.proofs-test/a-plan-reads-the-kept-program-db-of-its-tree
                      seon.proofs-test/a-kept-tree-costs-its-lookup-not-its-program}}]
